<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκθνῄσκω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θᾰνοῦμαι</span> : aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξέθᾰνον</span> :—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>die away, to be like to die,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέλῳ</span> (for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέλωτι</span>) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκθανον</span>
			<i>were like to die</i> with laughing, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.100
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρῶντες ἐξέθνῃσκον ἐπὶ τῷ πράγματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					190.7
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ γέλωτος ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.54c
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τοῦ δέους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Icar.</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be in a death-like swoon,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξέθανε πεντάκις ὥστε τεθνάναι δοκέειν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				5.42
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				1.6
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἐκτεθνεώς,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ὄντως τεθνηκώς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				959a
			</span></i> ; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποθνῄσκειν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				521a11
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				962b4
			</span></i>:—so in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				568
			</span></i> (though Nessus was really dying) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκθνῄσκων</span> may retain its usual sense, <i>fainting
				away, at the point of death.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>become mortified,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φλεγμαῖνον ἐκτέθνηκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>VC</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> c.acc., <i>to
				be terrified of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς νόσους ἐκτεθνήκασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Herc.</u>
					1251.18
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
				later,=<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποθνῄσκω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				2.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				48.37
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
